From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 06:08:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 303/311] avcodec/mpeg4videodec: do not round the GMC1 average
 MV with a zero shift

RSHIFT(x, 0) evaluates to x - 1 for negative x (the rounding term
(1 << 0) >> 1 is 0, but the negative branch still subtracts 1). With
a == 0 the GMC1 sum is exact, so use it unshifted.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 libavcodec/mpeg4videodec.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/mpeg4videodec.c b/libavcodec/mpeg4videodec.c
index cc97f64ba4..19009f6582 100644
--- a/libavcodec/mpeg4videodec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mpeg4videodec.c
@@ -861,7 +861,8 @@ static inline int get_amv(Mpeg4DecContext *ctx, int n)
         if (ctx->divx_version == 500 && ctx->divx_build == 413 && a >= s->quarter_sample)
             sum = ctx->sprite_offset[0][n] / (1 << (a - s->quarter_sample));
         else
-            sum = RSHIFT(ctx->sprite_offset[0][n] * (1 << s->quarter_sample), a);
+            sum = a ? RSHIFT(ctx->sprite_offset[0][n] * (1 << s->quarter_sample), a)
+                    : ctx->sprite_offset[0][n] * (1 << s->quarter_sample);
     } else {
         dx    = ctx->sprite_delta[n][0];
         dy    = ctx->sprite_delta[n][1];
